{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_no_hours_or_overtime_field", "label": "No hours, overtime or timesheet field", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The organisation does not operate overtime; a field for it implies a time-tracking regime that does not exist. Team load is WIP plus unplanned work derived from status. A metric that needs effort data is the wrong metric."}, {"id": "claude_never_rank_individuals", "label": "Never rank or compare individuals", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Throughput is a property of the system, not the person; the data cannot support the claim and the first report that makes it is the last one read. Ownership counts are fine, league tables are not."}, {"id": "claude_no_priority_score", "label": "Never compute a priority score", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "WSJF and its family multiply an unvalidated value estimate by an unvalidated size estimate and present the product as arithmetic. The delivery consequence of an ordering is computable and must be returned; relative worth stays with the people accountable."}, {"id": "claude_value_basis_is_prose", "label": "Value basis is free text carried to a reader", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A sentence a reader can argue with, carried through sequence() untouched. An enumerated basis is one join away from a table of weights, which is the same score arriving under a nicer name."}, {"id": "claude_agent_never_does_arithmetic", "label": "The agent never does arithmetic", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every figure comes from a tool; the agent quotes. Enforced structurally so a report is auditable; the moment the agent computes a percentage, nothing in it can be traced to one line of code."}, {"id": "claude_no_arithmetic_between_tools_and_reader", "label": "Nothing between the tools and a reader may do arithmetic", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "service/app.py and the Forge resolver validate, delegate and pass figures through; test_service asserts the service answer equals the tool byte for byte. A wrapper that computes one percentage is a second implementation, and the day it disagrees every number becomes something to check."}, {"id": "claude_one_contract_two_transports", "label": "Live mode: one contract, two transports", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The page asks by route name and gets {ok,status,body}; bodies are the contract, status is transport-level. src/app.js must never learn which transport it has or import @forge/bridge; the adapter is linked only into the split build."}, {"id": "claude_zero_network_zero_storage", "label": "Built file makes zero network calls and uses zero browser storage", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The threat model is that the file gets emailed. No CDN, fonts, analytics, localStorage or cookies; the security suite asserts all of it."}, {"id": "claude_credentials_only_in_fetcher_env", "label": "Credentials live only in the fetcher's environment", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": ".env, .jira-oauth.json (mode 0600) and data/dashboard-data.json are git-ignored; live server and OAuth listener bind 127.0.0.1 only; OAuth scopes read-only. Security suite asserts each by name."}, {"id": "claude_read_only_scope_allow_list", "label": "Every Forge scope read-only except two named ones", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "send:notification:jira and storage:app are allow-listed with a justification in the manifest, checked by test_service. Stricter than startswith('read:'), which would wave through every read scope Atlassian adds."}, {"id": "claude_major_version_rule", "label": "Module type or scope change is a major version", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Major stops forge deploy for --approve MAJOR_VERSION_RULE and needs forge install --upgrade (not an uninstall). Another entry under a block already declared is minor; the over-broad 'declaring a module always is' put a wrong cost into an ADR. Check by deploying. Free only while the sole install is development; hostnames and realms are the costliest entries after that window."}, {"id": "claude_refusals_printed_verbatim", "label": "Refusals are printed verbatim, never softened", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'Not enough data' and 'wide interval' are different statements and only one is true. Every refusal ends with 'the evidence is absent, not noisy'; that clause is the point."}, {"id": "claude_empty_selection_is_a_refusal", "label": "An empty selection is a refusal, not a zero", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Over zero issues a share has no denominator; divide-by-zero guards return good news. The health score printed 66/100 for an empty page. Inside a composite an unmeasurable component is dropped and named, survivors re-weighted, and below half the weight the composite refuses. Say which cause."}, {"id": "claude_org_config_travels_inside_data", "label": "Organisation config travels inside the data", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Done statuses, working days, holidays and sprint length are resolved once by the producer and written as orgConfig; no consumer opens config/organisation.json. src/app.js mirrors orgconfig.py and e2e asserts agreement under a non-default config. On Forge the resolver resolves from Jira status categories plus a project property."}, {"id": "claude_every_figure_carries_its_unit", "label": "Every figure carries its unit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Elapsed time in calendar days; simulated time in working days. The two disagreeing silently shipped once as 25% vs 22% flow efficiency for one sprint."}, {"id": "claude_value_counted_at_one_level", "label": "Business value counted at one hierarchy level", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An epic worth 40k and five stories at 8k are one piece of value and six rows; summing both reports 80k. valueFromHierarchy defaults to 1 and value_of() is the only reader; an issue with no level still counts."}, {"id": "claude_parent_and_subtasks_one_item", "label": "A parent and its subtasks are one item", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Item counting was chosen so the unit cannot be inflated; decomposing generously inflates it as estimating generously would. counted_issues() is the rule, countedIssues() mirrors it, and what was not counted is reported beside every figure."}, {"id": "claude_forecasts_in_items_not_points", "label": "Forecasts are in items, never story points", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Six sprints is six point-observations, which cannot support a distribution; the same sprints hold roughly sixty items. Points toggle is display only."}, {"id": "claude_seeded_reproducible_monte_carlo", "label": "Monte Carlo is seeded and reproducible", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fixed SEED, 20,000 trials. A forecast that moves when nothing changed is not a forecast."}, {"id": "claude_zero_throughput_days_stay_in_sample", "label": "Zero-throughput days stay in the sample", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dropping them is the most common way a Monte Carlo turns optimistic; a model that never samples zero never predicts a stall."}, {"id": "claude_refusal_thresholds_are_hard", "label": "Refusal thresholds are hard, not advisory", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Below them the honest answer is 'not enough data', not a wider interval. Listed in docs/forecasting-agent.md \u00a75 and docs/product-intake.md."}, {"id": "claude_no_silent_caps", "label": "No silent caps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Any top-N, truncation or sampling must say what was dropped; a truncated list reads as complete. Bit twice: a readiness printer showing four gaps while the summary counted five, and a backtest that overlapped its windows."}, {"id": "claude_ui_tokens_separate_from_chart_palette", "label": "UI colour tokens separate from chart palette", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "--link, --accent-bg, --info-ink exist so contrast fixes never touch series colours, which are validated for colour-vision deficiency independently."}, {"id": "claude_escape_at_output_once", "label": "Escape at output, once", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "All issue-derived strings pass through one esc() at output and URLs through safeUrl(); a Jira summary is writable by anyone who can raise a ticket. A stored XSS shipped from two call sites interpolating i.key and i.summary directly."}, {"id": "claude_plausible_wrong_number_failure_class", "label": "The plausible wrong number failure class", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A bug that returns a plausible wrong number rather than failing is the worst failure mode: a forecast computed against the wrong slice looks exactly like a correct one. Three shipped in the intake work (CHANGELOG 1.8.0). Say so loudly."}, {"id": "claude_dist_is_committed", "label": "dist/ is committed on purpose", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "So the repository is usable without a build step; CI fails if dist/ is stale, so a src/ change and its build are committed together."}, {"id": "claude_add_the_test_before_claiming_the_fix", "label": "Add the test before you claim the fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every 'found and fixed' changelog entry has a test pinning it; that is why the list is trustworthy. Changelog entries are prose recording the decision and the bug that prompted it."}, {"id": "claude_calculator_redeploys_on_push", "label": "Pushing service/** or agent/tools/** redeploys the calculator", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A resolver calling a route that only exists locally answers 404 until the push lands; push first, then forge deploy."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0008_forge_calls_a_hosted_calculator", "label": "ADR 0008: Forge calls a hosted calculator", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0009_one_contract_two_transports", "label": "ADR 0009: One contract, two transports", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0010_an_empty_selection_is_a_refusal", "label": "ADR 0010: An empty selection is a refusal", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0011_a_kanban_context_is_a_window_not_a_clock", "label": "ADR 0011: A kanban context is a window not a clock", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends", "label": "ADR 0014: Jira sends the brief and the read-only rule bends", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0015_a_durable_series_stores_what_jira_forgets", "label": "ADR 0015: A durable series stores what Jira forgets", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0018_permission_mirroring_holds_by_accident_and_where_it_does_not", "label": "ADR 0018: Permission mirroring holds by accident", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0024_a_parent_and_its_subtasks_are_one_piece_of_work", "label": "ADR 0024: A parent and its subtasks are one piece of work", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0025_the_app_declares_a_business_value_field", "label": "ADR 0025: The app declares a business value field", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0026_items_and_value_are_counted_from_two_different_sets", "label": "ADR 0026: Items and value are counted from two different 